# Normalize line endings: store text as LF in the repo regardless of the
# checkout platform. Without this, Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) plus
# tools that write LF (e.g. Prettier's default endOfLine) flip CRLF<->LF and
# produce massive phantom diffs. `text=auto` lets Git decide what's text;
# `eol=lf` pins the in-repo (and working-tree) ending to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
